 "answer": "# Part A: 95^445 mod 163\n\nSince 163 is prime, by Fermat's Little Theorem, 95^162 \u2261 1 (mod 163).\n445 mod 162 = 121, so we need 95^121 mod 163.\n\nComputing powers by repeated squaring:\n- 95\u00b2 \u2261 60\n- 95\u2074 \u2261 14\n- 95\u2078 \u2261 33\n- 95\u00b9\u2076 \u2261 111\n- 95\u00b3\u00b2 \u2261 96\n- 95\u2076\u2074 \u2261 88\n\nSince 121 = 64+32+16+8+1:\n95^121 \u2261 88 \u00b7 96 \u00b7 111 \u00b7 33 \u00b7 95 (mod 163)\n\nStep by step:\n- 88\u00b796 = 8448 \u2261 135\n- 135\u00b7111 = 14985 \u2261 152\n- 152\u00b733 = 5016 \u2261 126\n- 126\u00b795 = 11970 \u2261 71\n\n**Remainder = 71**\n\n# Part B: Product and digit sum\n\nStep 1: 92800 \u00d7 2872 = 266,521,600\n\nStep 2: 266,521,600 \u00d7 697\n= 266,521,600\u00d7700 \u2212 266,521,600\u00d73\n= 186,565,120,000 \u2212 799,564,800\n= 185,765,555,200\n\nStep 3: 185,765,555,200 \u00d7 5249\nUsing 5249 = 5250 \u2212 1:\n- \u00d75250 = \u00d75000 + \u00d7250 = 928,827,776,000,000 + 46,441,388,800,000 = 975,269,164,800,000\n- Subtract \u00d71: 975,269,164,800,000 \u2212 185,765,555,200 = 975,083,399,244,800\n\nFinal product: **975,083,399,244,800**\n\nDigit sum: 9+7+5+0+8+3+3+9+9+2+4+4+8+0+0 = **71**\n\n# Part C: CRT problem\n\nNeed x \u2261 3 (mod 7), x \u2261 0 (mod 9), x \u2261 3 (mod 5).\n\nLet x = 9k.\n- 9k \u2261 3 (mod 7) \u2192 2k \u2261 3 (mod 7) \u2192 k \u2261 5 (mod 7)\n- 9k \u2261 3 (mod 5) \u2192 4k \u2261 3 (mod 5) \u2192 k \u2261 2 (mod 5)\n\nSolve k \u2261 5 (mod 7), k \u2261 2 (mod 5):\nk = 7m+5 \u2192 7m+5 \u2261 2 (mod 5) \u2192 2m \u2261 2 (mod 5) \u2192 m \u2261 1 (mod 5)\nSo k = 35n + 12, giving x = 9k = 315n + 108.\n\nSmallest positive x (n=0): **x = 108**\n\nCheck: 108 = 15\u00d77+3 \u2713; 108 = 12\u00d79 \u2713; 108 = 21\u00d75+3 \u2713\n\nFINAL: 71; 71; 108"
